Gate ICMP on the same policy as a dial

Upstream forwards ICMP echo requests unconditionally. That left a path
out of a sandbox that sandbox reports as reaching nothing: with no allow
rules at all, the guest pinged 1.1.1.1 and got a reply, and nothing was
written to the audit log. An echo request carries a payload and elicits a
reply, so it is both a reachability oracle and a channel out.

There is no port, so the dial is gated at port 0: a bare rule matches
that, while a rule written with a port is about that port and does not
grant ping.

diff --git a/pkg/services/forwarder/icmp.go b/pkg/services/forwarder/icmp.go
